// # Ooda CLI — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Front door for the ooda/ directory's product CLI. The 4 subdirs are the in-process command implementations; main.oo is the argv router that also spawns the opm/lsp/mcp binaries.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. The 4 subdirs are: build, fix, fmt, token. main.oo is the cli/ entry point — parse argv, dispatch to one of the 4 subdirs or spawn opm/lsp/mcp.
//
// Beats:
//   1. The 4 in-process subdirs: build, fix, fmt, token. api_surface=4.
//
// v0.2.1: oodar is an independent polyrepo sibling. The build's runtime-root
// resolution now goes through `find_runtime_root(env)` (OODA_RUNTIME_ROOT
// env var, defaulting to src_root+"/oodar" per the polyrepo convention).
// Previously hard-coded to src_root+"/runtime/chs_rt.c" — that path has
// not existed since the oodar extraction (v0.1.0).
//   2. main.oo is the argv router: handles 12+ subcommands across the 4 subdirs plus 3 spawn entries (opm, lsp, mcp).
//   3. qa/, scripts/, docs/, examples/, VERSION provide the OPM tactical-subsystem template surfaces.
//   4. The cli/ repo's binary IS the `ooda` command. The 3 spawn entries (opm, lsp, mcp) keep version decoupling — the `ooda` binary does not link any of the 3 packages.

import "build/ANCHOR.oo";
import "fix/ANCHOR.oo";
import "fmt/ANCHOR.oo";
import "token/ANCHOR.oo";
